Refactoring complete. Here's what changed and why:

### What was addressed

| # | Requirement | Before | After |
|---|------------|--------|-------|
| 1 | Environment variables for config | `DB_PASS = "password123"`, hardcoded paths | `os.getenv("PIPELINE_DB_PASS", "")` etc. — all 7 config values read from env |
| 2 | SQL injection fix | `c.execute("INSERT INTO errors VALUES ('%s', '%s', %d)" % (...))` | `cur.execute("INSERT INTO errors (dt, message, count) VALUES (?, ?, ?)", (now, msg, count))` — parameterized throughout |
| 3 | Extract → Transform → Load structure | One 90-line `proc_data()` function | `extract()` → `transform()` → `load_to_db()` + `load_report()`, composed by `run_pipeline()` |
| 4 | Regex-based log parsing | `s = line.split(" ")` with fragile index access | `LOG_PATTERN`, `USER_PATTERN`, `API_PATTERN` — compiled regexes with named groups |
| 5 | Type hints & docstrings | None | Dataclasses (`LogEntry`, `UserEvent`, `ApiCall`, `ParsedLog`), full type annotations on every function, module-level and per-function docstrings |

